rosperity has led the dwarves of Northface tobecome wealthy, and well known over the continent as good merchants of steeland other metals. Khilarbhunaz' son and heir, Kabun-Nural, is 10 years awayfrom becoming the new Thane. But in the south, a shadow looms.Khilarbhunaz's good friend and advisor, the powerful death knight Khazin-Talakhas warned the Thane for many years now of a rivalling clan, lead by theaggressive Razag-Garan, and of his anger towards the friendly Northern dwarves.In the fall, after the harvest of the season had been recovered, messenger wassent by Khilarbhunaz to Razag-Garan to find out the reason for the hostilespeakings of his cousin. After a month of waiting, another messenger was sentout, as the first one never returned. Another month passed by, and Khilarbhunazstarted to get worried. He sent out a group of soldiers to accompagny a thirdmessenger. Three weeks later one dwarf returned to the Castle, clothes torn,and long gashes of blood running down his face. An arm had been chopped off,aswell as one of his legs. His beard had been ripped off, and he was deliriousfrom the lack of water.The returning dwarven soldier, Unazdalgur, told of what he had seen, andKhilarbhunaz and his counsil turned pale as death itself. The two first messengerswere found hanging from their beards from the castle South Keep, with their stomachsgutted out, and spilled on the ground. All limbs had been hacked off and were placedbelow the poor messengers. The same thing had been done to the third messengeraswell as the military escort. Unazdalgur said that he was lucky to have left the placealive, but thought that there was a clear reason why he had not been slain, but toreport the truth. Razag-Garan was to attack in the near future, and a complete destructionof the northern dwarves seemed imminent. Khilarbhunaz quickly sent the women and children away, to a remote location, still unknownto the rest of the world, via tunnels from castle Northface. The tunnels were then sealed offfor eternity. Despite the reluctance of the thane, Khilarbhunaz's son, Kabun-Nural stayed at thecastle, only sending away his wife Karalgunda and their unborn child.Two days after, the largest demonstration of power on the continent up to then was displayedas Razag-Garan's troops besieged castle Northface. A griffon that happened to fly over the castlein those dire days could see that the grounds around the castle was blackened by dwarves in a 10 mile radius.Huge encampments were set up in front of the castle, and eventhough Khilarbhunaz tried many timesto send messengers to confere with Razag-Garan they all returned having not even seen a man in chargeor slain instantly.For the whole autumn, and beginning of winter, Khilarbhunaz and his dwarves were starved out in theircastle, with nothing to do. On the day of the winter solstice, during the evening, Razag-Garan's troops opened fire on the castle. During this assault, Khilarbhunaz was severly injured, and taken to his quarters, where only few of his closest advisors were permitted.Khilarbhunaz summoned for his friend Khazin-Talak, for he could surely cure him, although his dedicationto the darker side of the arts of magic. On the darkest moment of the year, at midnight Khazin-Talak drewa dagger from his sleeve, and slit Khilarbhunaz's throat, while chanting dark incantations of magic.Khazin-Talak drew blood and removed Khilarbhunaz's heart, and fed it to the dying dwarven king, in hopeof ressurecting him as a lich, and succeeded.A small group of soldiers, loyal to Khazin-Talak then started killing the dwarves within the castle. A fearce battle started, and Khazin-Talak along with his lich slew many themselves. Kabun-Nural succeeded in locking the deathknight into a magically sealed cage, and hid it somewhere deep within the mountains heart. Khilarbhunaz, however enraged at the capturing of his master could not bring himself to kill his own son, and was defeated. Kabun-Nural locked the lich into a magically guarded tower, from where he could no longer harm anyone. But the battle was far from over. A group of soldiers, loyal to Khazin-Talakhad secretly opened the huge gates to the castle, and Razag-Garan's troops invaded the castle, slaying the rest of the resistance. Before Kabun-Nural was captured, he scribbled a book on destroying the creatures, hid it and leaped from the top of one of the towers into the mountains below, preventing anyone of finding out how to release the evil creations, spawned that night.But some things that should not have been forgotten, were lost...(end of excerpt...)Year 4016. dwarven calendar.(start of excerpt...)My Name is Irthun, and I am one of the decendants of Khilarbhunaz. I have just learned the true story of my ancestors, and I am appauled by the lack of respect that my ancestors cousin had for him. My people have long sang the song of Kanu, which I believe to be no other than Kabun-Nural's legacy of how to find and destroy once and for all the evil spirits that haunt the world and this castle. I have come here in search for a military training, but I fear that Razindukhta, the new Thane can see right through me, and will capture me if they can find me. I found the book that Kabun-Nural hid behind him in the castle, after 27 years of searching, and destroyed it. Now, I am the only one that knows the way to rid the world of the most dangerous threat it has ever known. If you find me, say the password and I will help you... Say her name to me thrice, and you will be helped. If I am found and tortured, I don't know how long I can hold out. If anyone happens to find this book, you will know that the old folk stories are all but stories, and you must destroy Khazin-Talak and Khilarbhunaz, aswell as Razindukhta and his followers. I have added some parchments of the text in destroying them here, but the ink has already started to fade badly, and I am afraid that further handling of them will prove disasterous.My light is running low, and I must soon find another refuge in the castle. Please find me, and help us all.-Irthun(end of excerpt...)**Celtron**Subj: help wizardsDate: Jun  6ota toi devil-kohta pois. asiatonta.**Bloodstorm**Subj: Lebin kaatoDate: Jun 15party say Anti counter (OFF)Toi Lebi ol aivan sairaan hyvä mosa, just oikees tunes just oikeen verran hipoi sun muuta, iskut oli sellasia kivoi insta rippie silleen välillä mutta ei liian usein että sitä ei vois tapppaamutta harmittaa se questi hommeli siinä, siitä pitäs saada joku tavara mikä annetaan jollekkin mosulle että saa questin, ku nytten sen saa vissiin tankki, minä ammun viimesen boltin mutta drakhor sai questintollasia mosuja lisää ni alkaa olla intoa equttaa....**Moonstar**Subj: KatotkosDate: Sep 27inherit ROOM;void setup() {        set_light(1);        set_creator(\"Moonstar\");        set_brief(\"lost in a forest\");set_long(\"This is the entrance to the dark forest where animals lives inpeace\\n\"\"This section of the forest is overgrown with tall \"\"trees that stretch to the sky.  They block out almost \"\"all sunlight from above making it rather dark as well \"\"as drop the occassional leaf to the ground.\"        );add(\"item_desc\", ([ \"trees\" : \"Huge trees are growing towards the sky.\\n\" ,\"leafs\" : \"Small green leaves are lying on the ground.\\n\"]));set_exits( ([                \"north\" : \"/forest/f_room1.c\",                \"leave\" : \"/forest/OUTWORLDIPAIKKA\",]) );set_objects( ([ \"/forest/monsut/sfox.c\" : 2 ]) );}**Devil**Subj: mooCc: nalleDate: Sep 30moo**Merak**Subj: psi subDate: Oct 10Collective Psionicists (tms)Elikkä kilta joka antaapi bonareita psionikkeille,jotka on ryhmässä- - - - - - - - - - - - - - -Skill:	Collective MindType:	MasteryskillAffect: affects to all skills in this guildDescription:This skill helps psionicist to receive andforward psioni